docker inspect … DNSNames lists exactly which names resolve; add others with --network-alias.

134
00:10:39,300 --> 00:10:42,889
Can you show me EXPOSE vs publishing ports?

135
00:10:43,433 --> 00:10:46,420
EXPOSE 80 in a Dockerfile is documentation:

136
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:49,824
it records which port the application listens on.

137
00:10:49,824 --> 00:10:51,005
It opens nothing.

138
00:10:51,005 --> 00:10:58,369
Publishing (-p HOST:CONTAINER on docker run) is what makes a container port reachable from outside Docker:

139
00:10:58,369 --> 00:11:03,093
the engine forwards a port of the host to the port of the container.

140
00:11:04,833 --> 00:11:07,083
The image documents its port:

141
00:11:07,083 --> 00:11:09,255
Start it without publishing.

142
00:11:09,255 --> 00:11:12,978
Another container reaches it; the host does not:

143
00:11:13,533 --> 00:11:15,702
Start it without publishing.

144
00:11:15,702 --> 00:11:19,420
Another container reaches it; the host does not:

145
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:21,511
docker port prints nothing:

146
00:11:21,511 --> 00:11:23,293
no host port is mapped.

147
00:11:23,833 --> 00:11:25,986
docker port prints nothing:

148
00:11:25,986 --> 00:11:27,819
no host port is mapped.

149
00:11:27,819 --> 00:11:30,928
Publish the port on a second container:

150
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:34,111
Let me try something.

151
00:11:34,111 --> 00:11:40,436
